    "headline": "Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued June 30 at 5:37PM CDT until June 30 at 6:30PM CDT by NWS Green Bay WI",
    "description": "SVRGRB\n\nThe National Weather Service in Green Bay has issued a\n\n* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...\nSouthern Oconto County in northeastern Wisconsin...\nEast Central Shawano County in northeastern Wisconsin...\n\n* Until 630 PM CDT.\n\n* At 537 PM CDT, a severe thunderstorm was located 7 miles northwest\nof Pulaski, or 12 miles east of Shawano, moving east at 35 mph.\n\nHAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and small hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.\n\n* This severe thunderstorm will be near...\nPulaski around 545 PM CDT.\n\nOther locations impacted by the severe thunderstorm include Zachow,\nAdvance, Pulcifer, Bonduel, Krakow, Green Valley, Sampson, Morgan,\nChase and South Chase.",
    "instruction": "Seek shelter inside a well-built structure and stay away from\nwindows. This storm is capable of producing damaging winds.",
    "response": "Shelter",
