    "senderName": "NWS Great Falls MT",
    "headline": "Flood Warning issued June 30 at 4:30PM MDT until July 1 at 4:30PM MDT by NWS Great Falls MT",
    "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Northwestern Glacier County in north central Montana...\n\n* WHEN...Until 430 PM MDT Wednesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 429 PM MDT, local law enforcement reported ongoing flooding in\nthe warned area.\n- Flooding impacts due to Swift Creek overflowing its banks will\ncontinue, but no additional rainfall is expected.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMany Glacier and adjacent areas.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
    "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nFlooding is occurring or is imminent. It is important to know where\nyou are relative to streams, rivers, or creeks which can become\nkillers in heavy rains. Boaters, campers, and hikers should avoid\nusing or going near streams or creeks.",
    "response": "Avoid",
    "note": null,
